    "created_at": "2017-04-24T11:18:19Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-04-24T11:18:19Z",
    "body": "The initial value of `returnValue` has no meaning, AFAICT from reading the spec, it's only meant to be assigned to after the event is fired.  So what's the point of initializing it?  I think it should have its own initializer only if we do that in other cases where it's pointless.  (Which offhand I suspect we do.)",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
