    "created_at": "2017-04-24T17:49:25Z",
    "updated_at": "2017-04-24T17:50:36Z",
    "body": "It allows authors to write unit tests on their beforeunload handlers, for example, or use frameworks that proxy events elsewhere by re-creating them, or similar. The issue is that authors shouldn't be using the beforeunload event, ideally---or at least, it's not clear it's worth four browsers' time to go from one state of interop (no constructor) to another (a constructor) when it's for a disfavored event anyway.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
